{
 "hash": "7a35d125995e",
 "id": "S08",
 "text": "Each walkway was carried by cross-beams called box beams. Each box beam was made from two C-shaped steel channels, welded edge to edge to form a hollow box. A steel rod passed through a hole in that box. Underneath, a nut and a washer held the beam up. All the weight of that section of walkway pressed down onto that one nut.",
